---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="DashFloat — a fast, robust CLI AI coding harness in Elixir"
  description="DashFloat streams LLM responses, executes structured tool calls, and manages coding sessions from the terminal. Built in Elixir on OTP."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>DashFloat</h1>
    <p class="tagline">A fast, robust CLI AI coding harness in Elixir.</p>
    <p class="sub">
      Streams LLM responses, executes structured tool calls, and manages coding
      sessions — from the terminal.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="cta primary" href="/docs/readme">Get started</a>
      <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/fluxvale/dashfloat">GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <ul class="cards">
      <li>
        <h3>Built on OTP</h3>
        <p>
          A pure render-loop UI process, an agent-manager GenServer, stream-handler
          tasks, and isolated subprocess execution — I/O never blocks rendering.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Terminal-native</h3>
        <p>
          An ex_ratatui TUI: a streaming markdown log, a live status bar, and a
          multi-line input with history, mouse selection, and clipboard copy.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Ships as one binary</h3>
        <p>
          burrito single-binary releases — no runtime to install, no bundles to
          untangle.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section quickstart">
    <h2>Quickstart</h2>
    <p class="status-note">
      Pre-alpha. Requires Elixir 1.20 and Erlang/OTP 29.
    </p>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/fluxvale/dashfloat.git
cd dashfloat
mix run --no-halt</code></pre>
    <p>
      Point it at any OpenAI-compatible provider in
      <code>~/.config/dashfloat/settings.json5</code> (API keys live in a sibling
      <code>keys.json5</code>, never in the settings file) — the
      <a href="/docs/readme">README</a> has the full setup guide.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Docs</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/docs/readme">README</a> and every
      <a href="/docs">architecture decision record</a> are rendered straight from
      the repository.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
